From: edwardzhu02 <explodingtnt@foxmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:10:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] stmp3770/hp39gii: add LCD text console device (/dev/lcdcon)

8x8 bitmap font + 32x16 text console rendered onto the 256x128 LCD
(1 byte per pixel). Registers /dev/lcdcon as a write-only character
device; the board LCD bring-up thread renders a test message through
it. This is the foundation for a real-hardware console (the HP 39gII
has no exposed UART, so NSH output needs the panel).

Rendering verified via EmuGII screendump pixel analysis (text glyphs
present in the top rows of the panel).
